sequenceDiagram
  %% Subtractive cleanup precedes record deletion. No provisioning, listener probes or environment writes.
  %% status: migrated
  %% command: instance:node-service:detach
  %% kind: instance.node_service_detach
  autonumber
  %% lane CALL icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  participant CALL as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>Control Node
  participant N as Instance Node<br/>Ansible
  Note over CALL: Resolve input and consent
  %%> When:
  %%> - Omitted Instance and attachment IDs use registry choices. The attachment GET is scoped to the selected Instance and completes before consent.
  %% path: local-invalid
  alt local input refused
    CALL--xCALL: Refused or cancelled<br/>No delete request
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - instance.id_invalid refuses an invalid supplied or missing noninteractive Instance ID, or an empty Instance list after the registry GET; no mutation request is sent.
    %%> - instance.node_service_target_id_invalid refuses an invalid supplied attachment ID, an omitted attachment ID in JSON or noninteractive mode, or an empty attachment list after its registry GET; no mutation request is sent.
    %%> - instance.node_service_confirmation_required refuses a JSON or noninteractive call without --yes.
    %%> - input.cancelled ends a cancelled terminal selection or confirmation, or declined consent, before mutation.
    %%> - State stays unchanged. Invalid supplied IDs, missing noninteractive IDs and missing noninteractive consent send no request. Terminal selection or confirmation cancellation can follow registry reads.
  else inputs and consent ready
    CALL->>GW: instance:node-service<br/>detach INSTANCE TARGET
    %%> Command:
    %%> - orbit instance:node-service:detach INSTANCE TARGET
    %%> - syntax: instance:node-service:detach
    Note over GW: Check request and access
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - peer.identity_unknown or node_access.required (403): the caller lacks authority.
    %%> - http.404 (404): the Instance cannot be resolved.
    %%> - validation.failed (422) or operation.idempotency_conflict (409): the request key is invalid or conflicts.
    %%> - Every refusal leaves state unchanged and creates no new receipt.
    alt request or access refused
      GW--xCALL: Request refused<br/>No changes or new receipt
    else request admitted
      Note over GW: Lock the Instance<br/>Begin one transaction
      alt lifecycle busy
        GW--xCALL: Lifecycle busy<br/>No changes or new receipt
        %%> On failure:
        %%> - instance.lifecycle_busy (409): the Instance is not active, migration is running or another detach on this Node is running.
      else failed move retains runtime
        GW--xCALL: Runtime cleanup required<br/>No changes or new receipt
        %%> On failure:
        %%> - instance.node_service_runtime_cleanup_required (409): retry instance:migrate to finish or restore the move before detaching.
      else target missing or foreign
        GW--xCALL: Attachment missing (404)<br/>No changes or new receipt
        %%> On failure:
        %%> - instance.node_service_target_missing: the attachment must belong to the selected Instance.
      else another Operation owns target
        GW--xCALL: Target busy<br/>No changes or new receipt
        %%> On failure:
        %%> - operation.target_busy (409): the Instance's Operation lock is held.
      else withdrawal transport unavailable
        GW--xCALL: Transport unavailable<br/>No changes or new receipt
        %%> On failure:
        %%> - For a container, swamp.ssh_target_unavailable or swamp.ssh_identity_unavailable (503), or swamp.node_missing (409), refuses missing pinned execution identity before admission.
      else target admitted
        alt checkout has no container runtime
          Note over GW: Remove attachment<br/>Record succeeded Operation
          alt transaction fails
            GW--xCALL: Transaction failed<br/>Both writes roll back
            %%> On failure:
            %%> - The attachment remains and no new receipt is persisted, including no failed receipt.
          else transaction commits
            GW-->>CALL: Completed Operation
          end
        else container runtime exists
          Note over GW: Capture withdrawal<br/>Record queued Operation
          %%> Why:
          %%> - The record retains the Process dependency until confirmed withdrawal, including on a migrated default.
          %%> - No service validation or listener probe is needed to revoke access.
          GW->>SW: Start withdrawal<br/>Native workflow
          GW-->>CALL: 202 Accepted<br/>CLI follows Operation
          SW->>SW: input
          %%> Why:
          %%> - The phase needs the pinned Node identity, selected tuple and shared ownership decisions.
          SW->>N: Revoke container access
          %%> When:
          %%> - timeout 300; Ansible tags access; no container start, stop, environment write or reach probe.
          %%> - Subtract the exact NIC grant and input rule only when no remaining attachment on this Instance uses that tuple.
          %%> - For the last Node user, retain every other persisted bridge tuple and call W's shared writer in withdrawal mode; newer admissions survive.
          %%> On failure:
          %%> - instance.node_service_runtime_missing refuses a missing container. instance.bridge_busy or a named bridge failure retains the record; already withdrawn access stays withdrawn.
          SW->>SW: Read access result
          %%> Why:
          %%> - Capture the phase's public result from the run file, including the failure code after a failed phase.
          SW->>SW: cleanup
          %%> When:
          %%> - After the phase and result read have completed, also on failure; remove the private run folder.
          SW-->>GW: Native terminal history<br/>Bound run and selected target
          alt run or withdrawal proof failed
            Note over GW: Retain attachment<br/>Record terminal failure
            GW--xCALL: Failed Operation<br/>Read code and retry detach
            %%> On failure:
            %%> - A new key starts an idempotent withdrawal attempt; replaying the failed key returns its original receipt.
            %%> - Partial withdrawal never authorizes record deletion. A late conflicting terminal cannot delete it.
          else withdrawal and run succeeded
            Note over GW: Delete attachment<br/>Commit success
            %%> When:
            %%> - Bound run identity, succeeded access phase and matching target result are required. Receipt and deletion share one transaction.
            GW-->>CALL: Completed Operation<br/>detached true
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
